.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.EX
#include \(dqserver.h\(dq

int pty_handle_spawn(int client_rfd, int client_wfd, const char *payload);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Handles a PTY spawn request received on \f[CR]CHAN_PTY\f[R] (channel 5).
This function is called from \f[CR]json_session_handle()\f[R] when a
client sends a \f[CR]{\(dqtype\(dq:\(dqspawn\(dq,...}\f[R] message.
It takes over the session event loop for the duration of the PTY
session.
.PP
\f[B]Sequence of operations:\f[R]
.IP "1." 3
Parses spawn parameters from the JSON \f[B]payload\f[R]:
\f[CR]rows\f[R], \f[CR]cols\f[R], \f[CR]shell\f[R], and
\f[CR]strip_ansi\f[R].
.IP "2." 3
Creates a pseudo\-terminal via \f[CR]forkpty()\f[R] and execs the
requested shell (default: \f[CR]/bin/bash\f[R]) as an interactive login
shell in the child process.
.IP "3." 3
Sends a \f[CR]spawn_ok\f[R] response frame with the allocated rows,
cols, and child PID.
.IP "4." 3
Enters the relay loop (\f[CR]pty_relay_loop()\f[R]), which uses
\f[CR]select()\f[R] to multiplex between client frames and PTY master fd
I/O.
.IP "5." 3
On exit (child terminates, client disconnects, or \f[CR]close\f[R]
message), sends an \f[CR]exit\f[R] frame with the child\(cqs exit code.
