.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
The relay loop handles \f[CR]CHAN_CONTROL\f[R] messages (ping,
disconnect) even while in PTY mode.
All other channels are ignored.
.IP \(bu 2
The child shell has \f[CR]TERM=xterm\-256color\f[R] set if
\f[CR]$TERM\f[R] is not already defined.
.IP \(bu 2
On child exit, remaining PTY output is drained and sent to the client
before the \f[CR]exit\f[R] frame.
.IP \(bu 2
The child is waited on with \f[CR]WNOHANG\f[R] polling.
If it does not exit within 5 seconds after the PTY master closes, it is
killed with \f[CR]SIGKILL\f[R].
